    "monitor.sources": "Sources:",
    "monitor.notice.prl": "Prolactin {value} ng/mL is above 3× the upper limit of normal you entered ({uln} ng/mL). MtF.wiki's stated action at this point is close observation and consideration of reducing the estrogen/progestogen dose, switching drug, or working up prolactinoma, which it describes as a repeat brain MRI. No source states a re-check interval.",
    "monitor.notice.alt": "ALT {value} U/L is above 2× the upper limit of normal you entered ({uln} U/L). FDA's CASODEX (bicalutamide) label is the only numeric action point found in the sources: discontinue immediately at ALT >2× ULN, with close follow-up of liver function. MtF.wiki states no multiple of ULN.",
    "monitor.notice.k": "Potassium {value} mmol/L is not below the 5.0 mmol/L the wiki requires before starting spironolactone; hyperkalemia is contraindicated. MtF.wiki states no re-check interval; the Endocrine Society's schedule is every 3 months for the first year, then annually.",
    "monitor.notice.cpa_cumulative": "Cumulative CPA: about {grams} g. At ≥10 g cumulative, MtF.wiki's recommendation is an MRI, while the Society for Endocrinology (SfE) recommends patient education and reserves urgent MRI for symptoms (vision loss, hearing loss, anosmia, tinnitus, seizures or limb weakness).",
    "monitor.recheck.title": "A re-check is due",
    "monitor.recheck.basis": "Basis: you first recorded a dose of {drug} on {date}.",
    "monitor.recheck.liver": "Liver function: for {drug} the interval is month {months} from your first recorded dose (monthly for the first 6 months).",
    "monitor.recheck.potassium": "Potassium: for {drug} the interval is month {months} from your first recorded dose (every 3 months for the first year, then annually).",
    "monitor.recheck.estradiol": "Estradiol (E2): a re-check is usually due about every 3 months; it is now month {months} since your first recorded {drug} dose. Confirm the exact interval with your doctor; you can change it in Settings.",
    "monitor.recheck.estradiol_check": "Estradiol (E2): a re-check is usually due about every 3 months; it is now month {months} since your last recorded test. Confirm the exact interval with your doctor; you can change it in Settings.",
    "monitor.recheck.basis_check": "Basis: your most recent recorded test was on {date}.",
    "monitor.recheck.weakness_check": "The start is your most recent logged test; any later test you did not log does not count.",
    "monitor.recheck.e2_interval": "MtF.wiki's US HRT review: “After levels stabilise, re-check about every 3 months.” Peking University Third Hospital: “After starting HRT, a re-check every three months is required to continue prescribing.” MtF.wiki's monitoring page, on liver function: “Check liver function once before starting treatment, and every three months during treatment.” These quote the usual practice; they are not an instruction.",
    "monitor.recheck.e2_trough": "The blood is drawn before the next dose. MtF.wiki: “Blood should be drawn close to before the next dose; do not check hormones immediately after taking the drug.” Most places follow the UCSF guideline, which measures sex hormones at the trough — just before the next dose — so a post-dose peak does not skew the clinical decision.",
    "monitor.recheck.e2_safety": "If you have severe mood or other problems, please consult a doctor as soon as possible.",
